# Bonsai 2 27B (ternary hybrid) - 1M context on one RTX 5090 (32 GB)
# Copy to .env and edit. Caller exports override this file (CONTEXT=262144 ./start.sh).

# --- model (edit this) -------------------------------------------------
# Which checkpoint to serve. The API alias follows this knob.
#   0 = base PQ2_0, PrismML, 2.13 bpw, 7.2 GiB weights
#   1 = abliterated PTQ1_0, BoldingBuilds, 1.75 bpw, 5.9 GiB weights
# Measured 2026-09-18 at 1M KV4: 132 t/s decode, 30.7 GiB idle VRAM (ablit).
ABLIT=1

# --- context -----------------------------------------------------------
# Tokens. Above 262144 REQUIRES patches/patch-gguf-context.py on the model
# file: llama-server caps slot context at n_ctx_train (the boot log says
# "capping") and silently re-partitions a bigger -c into 262K lanes instead.
# The yarn rope scale is derived from this value (1048576 -> x4.0).
CONTEXT=1048576

# --- kv cache ----------------------------------------------------------
# 1 = q4_0 KV cache + the mean-centering bias (make_kv_bias.sh in the demo
# repo; rebuild it per model file when you switch quants). 64 KiB/token fp16
# falls to 18 KiB/token q4: 1M KV = 17.9 GiB instead of 64. KV4=0 at
# CONTEXT=1048576 does not fit a 32 GB card.
KV4=1

# --- speculative decoding (optional, measured net-negative) ------------
# 1 = DFlash2 drafter (ProCreations, ~2.0 GiB VRAM). Measured 2026-09-18:
# acceptance 0.11-0.22 in every config tried, including the author's own
# prebuilt binary, vs 0.400 on their RTX PRO 6000 - so decode lands BELOW
# undrafted here (58-117 vs ~131 t/s). Forces CONTEXT<=921600. Full matrix
# in docs/BENCH.md.
DFLASH2=0

# --- serve -------------------------------------------------------------
# PARALLEL=1: one request owns the whole context; a second request during a
# long prefill gets a 503. 4 = four 262K lanes (which is also what an
# UNPATCHED GGUF at 1M turns into, via the slot cap).
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8013
PARALLEL=1

# --- overrides ---------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL: explicit GGUF path (beats ABLIT). ALIAS: API name override; the
# default follows ABLIT (Bonsai-2-27B-Ablit / Bonsai-2-27B). DEMO: the
# PrismML Bonsai-demo repo (launcher, models/, drafter).
# MODEL=
# ALIAS=
# TEMPLATE: chat template override. Default = files/bonsai2-template-tolerant.jinja
# (shipped): renders mid-conversation system messages as user turns instead of
# raising, which is what agentic clients (ZCode etc.) need. Empty = the
# template embedded in the GGUF (strict; 500s on late system messages).
# TEMPLATE=
DEMO=$HOME/Bonsai-demo
